{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BranchingPushforwardMultiplicativity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BranchingPushforwardMultiplicativity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.trM_tensor₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.trM_tensor₃","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BranchingPushforwardMultiplicativity.lean#L230-L234","doc":"**Three-body disjoint-union multiplicativity.**\n`tr_M((a ⊗ b) ⊗ c) = tr_M(a) tr_M(b) tr_M(c)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.weight_branching₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.weight_branching₃","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BranchingPushforwardMultiplicativity.lean#L213-L228","doc":"**The iterated weight identity.** `Σ_λ y_λ c^λ_{μνρ} = y_μ y_ν y_ρ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.branching₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.branching₃","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BranchingPushforwardMultiplicativity.lean#L191-L211","doc":"**The iterated restriction rule.** With `B'.D₁ = B.D` (the second branching's first\nfactor is the first branching's composite),\n`χ_λ((a ⊗ b) ⊗ c) = Σ_{μ,ν,ρ} c^λ_{μνρ} χ_μ(a) χ_ν(b) χ_ρ(c)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.c₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.c₃","kind":"def","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BranchingPushforwardMultiplicativity.lean#L169-L172","doc":"Three-factor branching multiplicities through the intermediate level:\n`c^λ_{μνρ} = Σ_κ c^κ_{μν} c^λ_{κρ}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.weighted_deviation_eq_of_trM_eq_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.weighted_deviation_eq_of_trM_eq_mul","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BranchingPushforwardMultiplicativity.lean#L140-L152","doc":"**The `y`-weighted deviation is pinned by any multiplicative bond law.** If the\ncomposite's trace is the free product's trace times a bond factor `bond` — the corpus's\n`tr_M(atom) = tr_M(free) · ∏(z_D + d_i)`, exact to ≤ 9e-51 on D, T, ³He, ⁴He\n(`branching_pushforward_entangled_support_probe.py`) — then\n`Σ_λ y_λ δ_λ = tr_M(a) tr_M(b) (bond − 1)`: the weighted total of the deviation is fixed by\nthe marginals and the bond product. Any objective on the composition program therefore\nsees only the *direction* of `δ` on that hyperplane, never its weighted total\n(bean `qou-ypc5`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.blockMass_tensor_char","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.blockMass_tensor_char","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BranchingPushforwardMultiplicativity.lean#L132-L138","doc":"The composite's block masses on a free product are determined by the two marginal\ncharacters through `c`: `y_λ χ_λ(a ⊗ b) = y_λ Σ c^λ_{μν} χ_μ(a) χ_ν(b)`. Stated so a reader\nsees that nothing in the free composite's block data goes beyond the inputs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.weighted_deviation_eq_zero_of_entangledSupp_empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.weighted_deviation_eq_zero_of_entangledSupp_empty","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BranchingPushforwardMultiplicativity.lean#L124-L130","doc":"The weighted deviation vanishes when no block separates `atom` from the free product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.trM_eq_tensor_add_weighted_deviation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.trM_eq_tensor_add_weighted_deviation","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BranchingPushforwardMultiplicativity.lean#L114-L122","doc":"**The trace of any composite element is the free product's trace plus the\n`y`-weighted entangled deviation.** Every binding form built from\n`tr_M(atom) / tr_M(free)` is therefore a function of `Σ_λ y_λ δ_λ` alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.deviation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.deviation","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BranchingPushforwardMultiplicativity.lean#L109-L112","doc":"The **entangled deviation** of a composite element from the free product of two\nmarginals, block by block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.trM_tensor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.trM_tensor","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BranchingPushforwardMultiplicativity.lean#L89-L107","doc":"**Disjoint-union multiplicativity, derived.** `tr_M(a ⊗ b) = tr_M(a) · tr_M(b)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.weight_branching","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.weight_branching","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BranchingPushforwardMultiplicativity.lean#L80-L80","doc":"The weight identity `Σ_λ y_λ c^λ_{μν} = y_μ y_ν`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.branching","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.branching","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BranchingPushforwardMultiplicativity.lean#L77-L77","doc":"The restriction rule for characters on a free product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.c","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.c","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BranchingPushforwardMultiplicativity.lean#L75-L75","doc":"Branching multiplicities `c^λ_{μν}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.tensor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.tensor","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BranchingPushforwardMultiplicativity.lean#L73-L73","doc":"The disjoint-union embedding `a ⊗ b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.D","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.D","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BranchingPushforwardMultiplicativity.lean#L71-L71","doc":"The pairing on the composite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.D₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.D₂","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BranchingPushforwardMultiplicativity.lean#L69-L69","doc":"The pairing on the second factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.D₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.D₁","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BranchingPushforwardMultiplicativity.lean#L67-L67","doc":"The pairing on the first factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BranchingPushforwardMultiplicativity.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData","kind":"structure","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BranchingPushforwardMultiplicativity.lean#L61-L80","doc":"Branching data: two Frobenius pairings embedded in a third through a\ndisjoint-union map, with branching multiplicities `c` and the weight identity. ","signatureChunk":0}]}